==Old English==

===Etymology===
From an earlier form {{m|ang|hlāfweard}}, from {{m|ang|hlāf}}) + {{m|ang|weard}}. Equivalent to {{m|en|loaf}} + {{m|en|ward}}. See also {{m|ang|hlǣfdīġe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhlɑːvord/|[ˈɬɑːvɔrd]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hlāford|m|hlāfordas}}

# [[lord]], master of servants
# male head of a household

